17. IMPORTANT DIFFERENCE:
   CART vs ORDER HISTORY
--------------------------------
Cart:

Purpose:
Stores what the customer currently wants to order.

Example:

cart = [
  product1,
  product2
]

After placing the order:

setCart([]);

The cart becomes empty.

Order History:

Purpose:
Stores orders that were already submitted/prepared.

Example:

orderHistory = [
  order2,
  order1
]

Clearing the cart does NOT clear orderHistory.


18. WHY ORDER HISTORY WAS PREVIOUSLY GIVING AN ERROR
----------------------------------------------------
The Order History popup was placed inside ProductCard().

But:

orderHistoryOpen

was declared inside:

Home()

Variables declared inside Home() are not directly available inside ProductCard().

This caused:

ReferenceError:
orderHistoryOpen is not defined

Correct structure:

Home()
 ├── orderHistory state
 ├── orderHistoryOpen state
 ├── Orders button
 ├── Order History popup
 ├── Category
 │    └── ProductCard
 └── other UI

The Order History popup must remain inside Home().


19. CURRENT LIMITATION
----------------------
This is a frontend-only Order History system.

The browser stores the data.

If the customer:
- changes device
- uses another browser
- clears localStorage
- uses another computer

the order history will not automatically appear there.

For a real production ordering system, Order History should eventually use:

Frontend
   ↓
POST Order API
   ↓
Backend
   ↓
Database
   ↓
User account / customer ID
   ↓
GET Order History API
   ↓
Frontend


